'''whit<sup>1</sup>''' (hwit), ''n.'' [A var. of *''wit'', a var. of ''wight'', < ME. ''wiȝt'', ''wiht'', sometimes ''with'', < AS. ''wiht'': see ''wight''<sup>1</sup>. The change of initial ''w-'' to ''wh-'' is perhaps due in this case to emphasis (so ''want''<sup>1</sup> is sometimes pronounced emphatically whont). The notion that ''whit'' is derived by metathesis from AS. ''wiht'' is erroneous.] The smallest part, particle, bit, or degree; a little; a jot, tittle, or iota: often used adverbially, and generally with a negative.
